% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's mixin `with_shared_window`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: the class body
% is lost (docs/simpos/subsystems/window.md §0.3, §1.3).  MENDELS (IFS
% No.61), 2026-11-27: the last nature of MENDELS's `base` (win_class.esp),
% and the create option nature([with_shared_window]) of its panes
% (mendel_win.esp); 11 held application classes have it (window.md §1.3).
%
% WHAT IS KNOWN: the name, read as WINCS's プロセス間共有, "shared between
% processes" (INFERENCE, window.md §1.3), and one held behaviour: cil
% calls :assign_window(W) before set_title, activate and deactivate of
% such a window (cil/src/ms_cfm.esp:118-128, USAGE).  INFERENCE: a window
% is registered to the process that made it (TM-125 p18 kill/1), and a
% shared one is taken over by the process that assigns it.  These
% stand-ins keep no window per process (OURS), so the assignment changes
% nothing.

class with_shared_window has

instance

% INTERPOLATED (selector USAGE cil ms_cfm.esp:118-128; body OURS): the
% window assigned to the sending process; nothing to do here (see the
% head).
% LABEL: INFERENCE (the meaning from the name and cil's use; no-op OURS)
:assign_window(W);

end.
